  "sees": "One forward camera (320 × 240, 110° wide, a new frame every 10 ms), the flight controller's gyro, accelerometer, attitude estimate, battery and rotor speeds, and the timing system's gate count. No position or speed.",
  "controls": "Acro commands, like a real pilot's sticks: throttle plus roll, pitch and yaw rates, 100 times a second, in real time.",
  "moment": "Final, race 2, 24 s in. Opus's drone is 4 m from gate 5, 1.5 s before it passes; Gemini's drone (yellow lights) is just above it and Astra's beyond the gate. On the broadcast each drone carries a coloured beacon (Opus green); the cameras on board see only the drones' own lights.",
  "camera": {
