  "details": [
   "Camera: one forward FPV camera, 320 × 240 pixels, 110° wide, tilted 30° up. It takes a frame every 10 ms; each image arrives 20 ms after it was taken, stamped with its step.",
   "IMU: the gyro and accelerometer of a racing flight controller, the latest 10 ms sample and the last 32, with noise, vibration and a new bias every race.",
   "Flight controller: its own attitude estimate, battery voltage, current and used capacity, and the four rotor speeds.",
   "Timing system: during a flight, the laps at gate 1, the number of gates passed in order and the next gate's number; the other gates' times after the flight.",
   "Referee: race and heat, time limit, points, standings, warnings, mid-air collisions, start slot, retirements and results.",
   "Not given: the drone's position or speed, where the gates are, a course map, or where the other drones are. The program finds its way from the camera and the IMU.",
   "Command: acro = throttle from 0 to 1, body rates for roll and pitch up to 670°/s and yaw up to 400°/s, and how long to hold them (0.01 to 1 s); after that the rates return to zero and the throttle stays.",
   "Timing: a control step every 10 ms; the race runs at real speed and never waits; a command acts at the next step, one command in flight at a time.",
   "Drone: a 5-inch racing quad (0.75 kg, 4S battery, rate mode at 500 Hz) held to the real drone's limits; the battery sags under load.",
   "Course: 8 gates in a 52 × 28 m hall, three laps; gates can carry moving shutters and blocking panels.",
   "Before the race: 60 minutes of preparation with a full practice copy of the course world and a practice racer. No GPU."
  ]
